From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:13:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Accept EAPOL from an associated station without wpa_sm

For an AP MLD, hostapd_event_eapol_rx() accepts only a station entry
with a wpa_sm when it looks up the BSS of the sender with
hostapd_find_by_sta(). A station that associated without RSN, such as
a WPS Enrollee, has none. The frame then goes to the BSS of the driver
event, which can be another link than that of the station. A non-MLO
station has no entry on the other links, and ieee802_1x_receive() drops
each EAP-Response.

Search again for any associated station entry when no entry with a
wpa_sm matches, as the handler did before commit a5188103220d ("AP MLD:
Handle link_id in EAPOL RX handler"). An entry with a wpa_sm keeps
priority.

Fixes: a5188103220d ("AP MLD: Handle link_id in EAPOL RX handler")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -2132,10 +2132,18 @@ static void hostapd_event_eapol_rx(struc
 				   int link_id)
 {
 	struct hostapd_data *orig_hapd = hapd;
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	struct hostapd_data *sta_hapd;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	hapd = switch_link_hapd(hapd, link_id);
-	hapd = hostapd_find_by_sta(hapd->iface, src, true, NULL);
+	sta_hapd = hostapd_find_by_sta(hapd->iface, src, true, NULL);
+	/* A station that associated without RSN, as a WPS Enrollee does, has
+	 * no wpa_sm. */
+	if (!sta_hapd)
+		sta_hapd = hostapd_find_by_sta(hapd->iface, src, false, NULL);
+	hapd = sta_hapd;
 #else /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	hapd = hostapd_find_by_sta(hapd->iface, src, false, NULL);
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
